From 5fdb087ee54012876b2a41c1f7e7b849580b09d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suharvest <suharvest@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 21:34:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 05/40] feat(asr): expose maxSessionBatchSize() on
 LLMInferenceRuntime for N>1 worker
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The N>1 ASR voice worker (qwen3_asr_worker.cpp) sizes its SessionLaneManager
to the engine's physical batch capacity via runtime->maxSessionBatchSize().
That accessor existed only on the deferred ASR-streaming spike's modified
runtime, not on the Base port branch, so the worker failed to compile:
  error: class LLMInferenceRuntime has no member named maxSessionBatchSize

Add the trivial read-only accessor (returns mDeployment.base.maxSupportedBatchSize,
the same field already used at llmInferenceRuntime.cpp:293). No streaming/runtime
state is introduced — it only exposes an existing deployment field, keeping the
deferred streaming wrapper out of the Base build.

With this + the minimal SessionLaneManager (prev commit), the ASR voice worker
compiles and links cleanly from this single integration branch
(targeted: cmake --build voice-workers --target qwen3_asr_worker → RC=0,
ARM aarch64 ELF, orin-nx).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 cpp/runtime/llmInferenceRuntime.h | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/cpp/runtime/llmInferenceRuntime.h b/cpp/runtime/llmInferenceRuntime.h
index 896618f..bf40267 100644
--- a/cpp/runtime/llmInferenceRuntime.h
+++ b/cpp/runtime/llmInferenceRuntime.h
@@ -209,6 +209,15 @@ public:
         return mDecoderRegistry && mDecoderRegistry->hasSpeculativeDecoder();
     }
 
+    //! @brief Number of physical batch lanes this runtime supports (KV capacity dimension).
+    //! @details Exposes the engine's maxSupportedBatchSize so the N>1 voice worker can size its
+    //!          SessionLaneManager to the engine's physical batch capacity. Read-only accessor on
+    //!          an existing deployment field — no streaming/runtime state involved.
+    int32_t maxSessionBatchSize() const noexcept
+    {
+        return mDeployment.base.maxSupportedBatchSize;
+    }
+
 private:
     //! @brief Common initialization logic shared between both constructors
     void initializeCommon(std::string const& engineDir, std::string const& multimodalEngineDir,
